Book will loose contact with the shelf when $\mathrm{a}=\mathrm{g}$.
Now $|\mathrm{a}|=\omega^{2} \mathrm{x} \therefore \mathrm{g}=\omega^{2} \mathrm{~A} \quad(\mathrm{~A} \rightarrow$ Amplitude)

\begin{array}{l}
\omega^{2}=\frac{g}{A} \text { also } f=\frac{\omega}{2 \pi} \\
\therefore f=\frac{1}{2 \pi} \sqrt{\frac{g}{A}}
\end{array}

replacing $\mathrm{g}=10 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s}^{2}$ and $\mathrm{A}=2.5 \times 10^{-2} \mathrm{~m}$
We get $\mathrm{f}=3.18 \mathrm{~Hz}$

